  "description": "Linux (ICINGA) to Windows (DC01) cross-boundary pivot. IcingaWeb2 CVE-2022-24716 file read → config creds → CVE-2022-24715 RCE → firejail CVE-2022-31214 → root → SSSD cache (matthew creds). Chisel tunnel to DC01 → ManageEngine CVE-2022-47966 SAML RCE → SYSTEM.",
  "introduction": "This scenario teaches cross-boundary pivoting from Linux to Windows across segmented networks. OSCP often tests your ability to chain footholds across different OSes.",
  "mental_model": "Treat dual-NIC hosts as bridges: root on Linux pivot gives you internal network access via tunneling. Always check SSSD/cache for domain creds.",
  "key_principles": [
    "LFI often leads to config files with creds",
    "Dual-NIC hosts are pivot points between networks",
    "Chisel reverse tunnel exposes internal ports to Kali",
    "SSSD cache dumps reveal domain user passwords",
    "ManageEngine products often have unauthenticated RCE"
  ],

